https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T20:12:28Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T20:12:28Z","body":"I can confirm the issue. From the errors and only happen with the combo of Intel GPU + D3D12 seems to be the same case as #118719","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4870091272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5158153955","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120857#issuecomment-5158153955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120857","id":5158153955,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM3Mu4w","user":{"login":"Wagnard","id":11493785,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDkzNzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11493785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard","html_url":"https://github.com/Wagnard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T13:19:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T13:19:07Z","body":"Update: two distinct triggers isolated, both on non-opaque materials\nI chased this down in my project until it stopped crashing. There turned out to be two separate triggers, not one. Both involve materials that are not plain opaque.\n\nTrigger 1 — visibility_range_fade_mode = VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_SELF\nSetting this to VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED fixed two independent crashes.\n\nImportant: I did not touch visibility_range_begin / visibility_range_end. Range-based culling is still fully active everywhere (foliage still culls at 175 m, props at 75 m). Only the dither fade path had to go. So the trigger is the fade rendering path specifically, not the visibility range feature.\n\nCase A — hundreds of instances. Foliage scattered with ProtonScatter using render_mode = Create Copies (per-node duplication of a PackedScene, not MultiMesh), several hundred resulting MeshInstance3D, alpha-scissor foliage material. Device removal happened immediately on entering the scene with no user interaction.\n\nCase B — a single instance. One MeshInstance3D (a campfire fire effect) with a transparent raymarching shader as material_override, visibility_range_end = 100.0, margin = 10.0. The node starts visible = false and is enabled when night falls in-game. It crashed while walking backwards away from it.\n\nCase B rules out instance count as the factor — one fading mesh is enough.\n\nTrigger 2 — alpha_cut = ALPHA_CUT_DISCARD on Sprite3D / Label3D\nThis one is independent of the first: it crashed with visibility_range_fade_mode already disabled.\n\nDropped-item pickups, each made of two Sprite3D and one Label3D, all with alpha_cut = 1 (Discard). Their textures and label text are assigned at runtime from the item's data.\n\nThe crash happens on first rasterization, not on instantiation. Most reproducible form: drop an item while facing away from it, then turn the camera so it enters the frustum — device removal within about a second of it becoming visible.\n\nChanging all three nodes to alpha_cut = 2 (ALPHA_CUT_OPAQUE_PREPASS) makes it stable. visibility_range_end was left at 100.0.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5158153955/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5158907963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120857#issuecomment-5158907963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120857","id":5158907963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM36wOw","user":{"login":"Wagnard","id":11493785,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDkzNzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11493785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard","html_url":"https://github.com/Wagnard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T15:34:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T15:34:30Z","body":"Update2 : the device is lost inside CreateGraphicsPipelineState\nI finally got a run where the error chain was captured before everything else fell over. Only the first line matters — every error after it is a D3D12 call failing because the device is already gone:\n\nERROR: Create(Graphics)PipelineState failed with error 0x887a0005.\n   at: (drivers/d3d12/rendering_device_driver_d3d12.cpp:5360)\nERROR: Condition \"!pipeline.driver_id\" is true. Returning: RID()\n   at: render_pipeline_create (servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp:4960)\nERROR: Condition \"pipeline.is_null()\" is true.\n   at: _create_pipeline (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/scene_shader_forward_clustered.cpp:506)\nERROR: CreateResource failed with error 0x887a0005.\n   at: (drivers/d3d12/rendering_device_driver_d3d12.cpp:1404)\nERROR: Condition \"!texture.driver_id\" is true. Returning: RID()\n   at: texture_create (servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp:1704)\nERROR: Condition \"texture.rd_texture.is_null()\" is true.\n   at: texture_2d_initialize (servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp:1042)\nERROR: Attempting to use an uninitialized RID\n   at: (./core/templates/rid_owner.h:247)\nThe device dies at or during graphics pipeline state creation — which on D3D12 is where the driver compiles the shader bytecode into native ISA.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5158907963/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703668447","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120857#issuecomment-5703668447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120857","id":5703668447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU_cS3w","user":{"login":"Wagnard","id":11493785,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDkzNzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11493785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard","html_url":"https://github.com/Wagnard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T19:57:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T19:57:10Z","body":"I can confirm that PR #122994 fixes the crash.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703668447/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]